WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.780
Olympus Mons.

00:02.480 --> 00:06.046
The largest volcano we know of on any planet.

00:06.496 --> 00:11.457
It is more than twenty kilometres high, and its base would cover Arizona.

00:11.907 --> 00:18.156
Mars has no moving plates, so the lava kept piling up in one place for a very long time.
